{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`**\n1. `Domain::source_node` receives the requested path and selector and returns `Self::NodeData`.\n2. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to get a `NodeId<Self>`.\n3. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error.\n4. The public trait signature is part of the API. It is anchored to `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `tests/public_api.rs`.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Error case.** `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` (`agent/project_sources.rs`) uses a test domain whose `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid(\"unsupported source item\")` in two cases:\n  - an unknown path (`unknown.txt`);\n  - an invalid selector (`line[unknown]`).\n\n  The test asserts that `read_source` returns an error containing that text. It also asserts that no dependency is recorded and that no node read happens (`reads == 0`, `read_nodes` empty). This covers the \"unsupported or invalid address returns an error\" obligation for both address components. The selector case also shows the selector reaches the domain.\n- **Successful mapping and interning.** The same test reads `source.txt` with an empty selector. The domain returns `\"source-node\"`, and the test asserts the following:\n  - the recorded dependency is `Dependency::Node(domain.cache().intern_node(\"source-node\".into()), returned.fingerprint())`, so the SDK interned the returned data in the domain cache;\n  - `read_nodes == [\"source-node\",\"source-node\"]`, so the read went through the interned node.\n\n  It then checks that the record goes stale when the content changes.\n- **Interning in discovery and search.** `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` (`agent/configured.rs`) drives `list_sources`, `search_text`, and `read_node` through a `TestDomain`. The domain logs each `OutlineData` it is asked to map, and the test asserts the logged items for `visible/selected.txt`. The test also asserts that the dependency list contains the interned `TestNode` ids 7, 8, 9 and 10. Those ids come from the domain's path-based mapping, so the SDK passes the right path and interns the result for listing and search hits. The test runs the scenario twice.\n- **Signature.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks the public export inventory against the book.\n\n**Unmarked default-implementation test**\n`tests/contracts.rs` also has a test that the default `Domain::source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`. It is marked for other requirements and not for this one. The subject text conditions its main obligation on \"an application supporting tracked source inspection\". It does not specify the default body, because the signature shows `{ ... }`. I treated that test as outside this requirement's marked obligations, not as a gap.\n\n**Passthrough code**\n`ValidationContext::read_source` in `procedure.rs` passes the `OutlineData` unchanged to `source_node` and then interns the result. It has no conditional logic of its own. The error and interning behavior is asserted in the tests above.\n\nNo unacknowledged adequacy gap found.",
